# Line endings, stated explicitly rather than left to each machine's
# core.autocrlf setting.
#
# This matters here: the launchers are .bat files, cmd.exe is unreliable with LF
# line endings inside parenthesised blocks, and a clone on a machine with
# autocrlf=false would otherwise check them out as LF and break them. Declaring it
# per-pattern removes the dependency on anyone's local config.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Never touch these. Git should not try to normalise a binary.
*.ico binary
*.png binary
*.zip binary
